# 10. Queue Behavior Example

Consider the following operations:

```text
ADD A FileA
ADD B FileB
ADD C FileC
```

The Queue should conceptually contain:

```text
FRONT
  ↓
[A] → [B] → [C]
              ↑
             REAR
```

Then:

```text
PRINT
```

processes `A`.

Queue becomes:

```text
FRONT
  ↓
[B] → [C]
       ↑
      REAR
```

Another:

```text
PRINT
```

processes `B`.

Queue becomes:

```text
FRONT
  ↓
[C]
 ↑
REAR
```

Therefore, the processing order must always be:

```text
A → B → C
```

